  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Finished Building",
    "overview": "The site presents like a serious construction or development company: the building is finished, photographed in good daylight, and handed over. A realistic render of the model is the default state and leads the first viewport; everything else steps back so it can be seen. The page is warm off-white with near-black type, one quiet forest green for commitment, and a great deal of air. Lines are rare and hairline; controls are few, grouped, and pill-shaped.\n\nThe model is lit as architecture, not as a product shot: a warm sun with soft shadows, a hemisphere sky, ambient occlusion in the corners, and neutral tone mapping so materials read at their true colour. The horizon and ground are tuned to the page background, so the canvas has no edge: the building sits on the page itself. Drawing conventions survive only where they carry information: solid charcoal poché where a section cut opens a wall, and faint grey ghost lines for the parts of the building lifted away.\n\nThe previous \"construction drawing set\" world (blue diazo ink, vellum, grid bubbles, title blocks, condensed caps) is retired and must not return.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Realistic render by default; White and Lines are alternative finishes, not the identity.",
      "Warm off-white page (#f5f5f3) continuous with the 3D horizon.",
      "One accent, forest green, reserved for commitment and selection.",
      "Wide-axis Archivo display, sentence case, tight tracking; plain Archivo for everything else.",
      "Pills for every control; hairlines for structure; almost no boxes."
    ],
    "rules": [
